## 3. THE INTERACTION: COLLAPSED ICON RAIL x THE FOOTER RULE x THE PAGE-JUMP FIX (your design, these fix the property)
**Property.** At 1024 px and up the footer's left padding follows the rail's real state, exactly: expanded = 228 + 24 = **252 px**; collapsed icon rail = rail width + 24; below 1024 px = as today (the drawer overlays nothing at the footer). The footer text is never under the rail, and no more than the gutter beyond it.
- **Rail width, collapsed: exactly 64 px, written in px like its 228 px sibling** (`lg:w-[64px]`, not `w-16`: the 228/252 pair is px, so the 64/88 pair is px; a rem width and a px padding would part at a 20 px root font). The kit's "72 px or less" in E2 becomes "64 px (+/- 1 px sub-pixel)". Footer collapsed = **88 px** (64 + 24).
- **A state hook that is not `inert`.** Add one attribute to the `aside` that exists only while `persistent && !open` (suggested `data-collapsed`; absent expanded, absent in the drawer in every state). The two footer variants must be **mutually exclusive** (expanded: `...:not([inert]):not([data-collapsed])` keeps `252px`; collapsed: `...[data-collapsed]` gives `88px`), so which wins is never the stylesheet's order (`Sidebar.tsx:65-67` records that lesson). Keep `lg:` on both. Any other mechanism (a body attribute, a context) that meets the property is allowed if it needs no JavaScript at layout time and keeps the footer in `layout.tsx` (a Server Component: it cannot read the sidebar's state).
- **The rail's content width.** The aside's inner wrapper is `px-2` (`Sidebar.tsx:72`): a 64 px rail leaves a 48 px link row; the link is `border-l-4 px-3` (`GlobalNav.tsx:108`, `CustomerNav.tsx:9`), leaving a 20 px content box for an 18 px icon (`ui/icons.tsx:6` default size 18). DERIVED at a 16 px root; **UNMEASURED at a 20 and 24 px root** (`px-3` is rem, the rail is px). So in the collapsed state centre the icon and drop the link's horizontal padding (an icon-only class set, not a script). **Keep the wrapper's 8 px side padding or more:** the outside ring reaches 5 px sideways and the aside is `overflow-y-auto` (so it clips on x too).
- **No page jump, collapsed.** The 64 px overhang and the height calc are the same classes, so the fix holds in principle; the existing trip heights do NOT: they were found against the EXPANDED rail's content height (`:652` 438/440/442, `:662` 738/740/742, `:670` 600, `:675` 770), and the collapsed rail is a different height (mode line and group labels go `sr-only`). Run collapsed at those heights the cells would be vacuous. **Recalibrate at base: sweep the window height 2 px at a time over the range where the current item's ring is within 5 px of the window edge, per role, and use the cells around the flip point; each cell needs a control that makes it red (the PM plant), printed.**
- **Hamburger placement** (kit DESIGN 2) is above the mode line, inside the rail, only when persistent; its 44 px target sits in the 48 px row. The mode line, group labels and link labels are `sr-only` text (never `aria-label`): the existing walks read `textContent` for the focused control's name (`:638`, `:708`), so an icon button with only an `aria-label` would loop to its 40-press cap.

